{"name":"Iolite","hex":"#7d89bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"iolite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The clear variety of cordierite, sometimes used as a gem."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iolite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cordierite","blocks":[{"text":"Cordierite (mineralogy) or iolite (gemology) is a magnesium iron aluminium cyclosilicate. Iron is almost always present, and a solid solution exists between Mg-rich cordierite and Fe-rich sekaninaite with a series formula: (Mg,Fe)2Al3(Si5AlO18) to (Fe,Mg)2Al3(Si5AlO18). A high-temperature polymorph exists, indialite, which is isostructural with beryl and has a random distribution of Al in the (Si,Al)6O18 rings. Cordierite is also synthesized and used in high temperature applications such as catalytic converters and pizza stones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Cordierite-den07-06aa.jpg/330px-Cordierite-den07-06aa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cordierite","wikidata":"Q410336"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Cordierite_structure.png/500px-Cordierite_structure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Cordierite_structure.png/500px-Cordierite_structure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crystal structure of Cordierite. Green – Mg or Fe, blue – O, yellow – Si and Al. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACordierite_structure.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Cordierite.jpg/120px-Cordierite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Cordierite.jpg/250px-Cordierite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm